#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The power plant is a <a object|power>power cell</a> factory. It transforms a"
" <a object|titan>titanium cube</a> into a regular power cell fully charged "
"and ready for use."
msgstr ""
"Questo impianto produce <a object|power>batterie</a>. Trasforma un <a "
"object|titan>cubo di titanio</a> in una batteria normale completamente "
"carica e pronta all’uso."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A power plant requires some energy in the subsoil. If the satellite report "
"says that energy is available only at some places, you will need a <a "
"object|botsr>sniffer bot</a> to prospect the subsoil. The marks it lays down"
" provide information about the specifics of its findings: a <a "
"object|enerspot>green cross</a> means that there is an energy deposit at "
"this location beneath the surface, which is indispensable for the "
"construction of a power plant or a <a object|station>power station</a>."
msgstr ""
"La fabbrica di batterie richiede energia nel sottosuolo. Se il rapporto "
"satellitare indica che l’energia è disponibile solo in alcuni punti, usa un "
"<a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> per individuarli. Una <a "
"object|enerspot>croce verde</a> segnala un deposito sotterraneo di energia, "
"indispensabile per costruire una fabbrica di batterie o una <a "
"object|station>centrale elettrica</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the large power cell at the base of the plant remains red after the "
"construction is completed, this means that the site is not geologically "
"adequate."
msgstr ""
"Se la grande batteria alla base dell’impianto resta rossa dopo la "
"costruzione, il sito non è geologicamente adatto."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat and geologically adequate surface of at least 4 meters wide."
msgstr ""
"Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante geologicamente adatta, larga almeno 4 "
"metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regular power cell."
msgstr "Batteria normale."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:19 ../E/station.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subsoil energy."
msgstr "Energia del sottosuolo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "12 seconds."
msgstr "12 secondi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/energy.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>PowerPlant</code>"
msgstr "<code>PowerPlant</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Underground Energy Deposit"
msgstr "Deposito sotterraneo di energia"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "enerspot"
msgstr "enerspot"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whenever a <a object|botsr>sniffer</a> uncovers a source of energy in the "
"subsoil, it lays down a green cross. The following buildings can be erected "
"nearby :"
msgstr ""
"Quando un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> scopre una fonte di energia "
"nel sottosuolo, la contrassegna con una croce verde. Nelle vicinanze puoi "
"costruire:"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|station>Power station</a>"
msgstr "<a object|station>Centrale elettrica</a>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|energy>Power plant</a>"
msgstr "<a object|energy>Fabbrica di batterie</a>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to prospect the subsoil you need a <a object|botsr>sniffer bot</a>,"
" which can also discover <a object|titanore>titanium ore</a> deposits "
"(indicated by a <a object|stonspot>red cross</a>) or <a "
"object|uranore>uranium ore</a> deposits (indicated by a <a "
"object|uranspot>yellow circle</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Per esaminare il sottosuolo serve un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a>, "
"che può trovare anche giacimenti di <a object|titanore>minerale di "
"titanio</a>, segnati da una <a object|stonspot>croce rossa</a>, o di <a "
"object|uranore>minerale di uranio</a>, segnati da un <a "
"object|uranspot>cerchio giallo</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:11 ../E/flag.txt:12 ../E/mine.txt:8 ../E/stonspot.txt:8
#: ../E/target2.txt:6 ../E/uranspot.txt:9 ../E/waypoint.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Impossible."
msgstr "Impossibile."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/enerspot.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>PowerSpot</code>"
msgstr "<code>PowerSpot</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/exchange.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 172/> Information Exchange Post"
msgstr "<button 172/> Centro di scambio dati"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/exchange.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "info"
msgstr "info"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/exchange.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This building stores digital information. A post can contain up to 10 pieces of information, each one referenced by a name.\n"
"For example, a post can contain 3 informations:<c/>\n"
"\\tab;\"Position.x\"  23.45\n"
"\\tab;\"Position.y\"  -102.70\n"
"\\tab;\"Quantity\"    3.00"
msgstr ""
"Questo edificio conserva informazioni digitali. Può contenere fino a 10 dati, ciascuno identificato da un nome.\n"
"Per esempio, un centro può contenere 3 dati:<c/>\n"
"\\tab;\"Position.x\"  23.45\n"
"\\tab;\"Position.y\"  -102.70\n"
"\\tab;\"Quantity\"    3.00"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/exchange.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To put new information, you must execute the command <code><a cbot|send>send</a></code>.\n"
"To read information from a post, you must execute the command <code><a cbot|receive>receive</a></code>."
msgstr ""
"Per inserire informazioni esegui il comando <code><a cbot|send>send</a></code>.\n"
"Per leggerle esegui il comando <code><a cbot|receive>receive</a></code>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/exchange.txt:13 ../E/radar.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat surface of at least 2.5 meters wide."
msgstr "Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante larga almeno 2,5 metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/exchange.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Digital information."
msgstr "Informazioni digitali."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/exchange.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>ExchangePost</code>"
msgstr "<code>ExchangePost</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/factory.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 160/> Bot Factory"
msgstr "<button 160/> Fabbrica di robot"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/factory.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "factory"
msgstr "factory"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This building is intended for the manufacturing of bots using <a "
"object|titan>titanium</a>."
msgstr ""
"Questo edificio produce robot utilizzando <a object|titan>titanio</a>."

#. type: Bullet: '1)'
#: ../E/factory.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Place the titanium cube inside the factory."
msgstr "Posa il cubo di titanio all’interno della fabbrica."

#. type: Bullet: '2)'
#: ../E/factory.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step back out."
msgstr "Esci dalla fabbrica."

#. type: Bullet: '3)'
#: ../E/factory.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the factory."
msgstr "Seleziona la fabbrica."

#. type: Bullet: '4)'
#: ../E/factory.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Click on the button showing the diagram of the bot you want the factory to "
"assemble (e.g. <button 137/> for a <a object|botgr>wheeled grabber</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Fai clic sul pulsante con lo schema del robot da assemblare (per esempio "
"<button 137/> per un <a object|botgr>robot trasportatore su ruote</a>)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The finished bot does not include an onboard <a object|power>power cell</a>."
" You'll need to supply it with one for it to be able to leave the factory."
msgstr ""
"Il robot prodotto non include una <a object|power>batteria</a>: devi "
"fornirgliene una perché possa uscire dalla fabbrica."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The list of feasible bots will depend upon the research your <a "
"object|research>research center</a> has completed at this time."
msgstr ""
"L’elenco dei robot producibili dipende dalle ricerche completate nel <a "
"object|research>centro di ricerca</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat surface of at least 7.5 meters wide."
msgstr "Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante larga almeno 7,5 metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "Completed bot."
msgstr "Robot completato."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/factory.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>BotFactory</code>"
msgstr "<code>BotFactory</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/flag.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colored Flag"
msgstr "Bandiera colorata"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/flag.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "flag"
msgstr "flag"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flag.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The colored flags are helpful to mark strategic locations or positions that "
"<a object|human>you</a> will need to find again. Flags appear on the mini-"
"map in the shape of a cross of the same color as the flag."
msgstr ""
"Le bandiere colorate servono a segnare luoghi strategici o posizioni che <a "
"object|human>dovrai</a> ritrovare. Sulla minimappa compaiono come croci "
"dello stesso colore."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flag.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the buttons <button 118/> and <button 119/> to plant and remove flags, "
"the colors of which you can choose with the buttons above."
msgstr ""
"Usa i pulsanti <button 118/> e <button 119/> per piantare e rimuovere le "
"bandiere. Puoi sceglierne il colore con i pulsanti superiori."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flag.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When your mini-map is out of order, the fact that flags follow the direction"
" of the wind can help you to find your way and not to walk around in "
"circles."
msgstr ""
"Quando la minimappa non funziona, le bandiere possono aiutarti a orientarti:"
" seguono la direzione del vento e ti permettono di evitare di girare in "
"tondo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flag.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When programming, you can use flags to give a bot a reference to a certain "
"position: the instruction <code><a cbot|radar>radar</a></code> allows bots "
"to know the exact position of a flag of a given color."
msgstr ""
"Nei programmi puoi usare le bandiere come riferimenti di posizione: "
"l’istruzione <code><a cbot|radar>radar</a></code> permette ai robot di "
"conoscere la posizione esatta di una bandiera di un determinato colore."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/flag.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>BlueFlag</code>\n"
"<code>RedFlag</code>\n"
"<code>GreenFlag</code>\n"
"<code>YellowFlag</code>\n"
"<code>VioletFlag</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code>BlueFlag</code>\n"
"<code>RedFlag</code>\n"
"<code>GreenFlag</code>\n"
"<code>YellowFlag</code>\n"
"<code>VioletFlag</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/goal.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finishing Pad"
msgstr "Piattaforma di arrivo"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/goal.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "The finishing pad is an objective to be reached in some exercises."
msgstr ""
"La piattaforma di arrivo è un obiettivo da raggiungere in alcuni esercizi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/goal.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>GoalArea</code>"
msgstr "<code>GoalArea</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/human.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 136/> Astronaut"
msgstr "<button 136/> Astronauta"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/human.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "human"
msgstr "human"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "The astronaut is you within the game."
msgstr "L’astronauta rappresenta te nel gioco."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you die, the mission immediately fails."
msgstr "Se muori, la missione fallisce immediatamente."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can construct buildings with the help of the neutron gun holstered to "
"your survival kit. The survival kit allows you, in most missions, to fly, "
"thanks to the reactor placed underneath, or to swim with no time limit. You "
"can carry most objects but the weight will slow down your movements "
"considerably. Flying, swimming and walking underwater are also made "
"impossible if you are carrying an object. The use of a <a "
"object|botgr>grabber</a> or a <a object|botsub>subber</a> is advised for "
"tasks such as these."
msgstr ""
"Puoi costruire edifici con la pistola a neutroni agganciata al kit di "
"sopravvivenza. Nella maggior parte delle missioni il kit ti permette di "
"volare, grazie al propulsore inferiore, e di nuotare senza limiti di tempo. "
"Puoi trasportare quasi tutti gli oggetti, ma il loro peso rallenta "
"notevolmente i movimenti. Quando trasporti qualcosa non puoi volare, nuotare"
" o camminare sott’acqua. Per questi compiti conviene usare un <a "
"object|botgr>robot trasportatore</a> o un <a object|botsub>robot "
"sommergibile</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You cannot carry <a object|uranore>uranium ore</a> because of the risks "
"attached to radioactivity. "
msgstr ""
"Non puoi trasportare <a object|uranore>minerale di uranio</a> a causa della "
"radioattività. "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A special button <button 111/> allows you to ensure that the ground around "
"you is flat. This is important since building is only possible on a flat "
"surface. A flat surface is designated green while a sloping one is red."
msgstr ""
"Il pulsante <button 111/> permette di controllare se il terreno circostante "
"è pianeggiante, condizione necessaria per costruire. Le aree pianeggianti "
"sono verdi, quelle in pendenza rosse."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A button <button 118/> allows you to mark a location with <a "
"object|flag>flags</a> of various colors. This can help you not to get lost, "
"to find important positions again, or to indicate a position to a bot. 5 "
"flags of 5 different colors are at your disposal. You can remove a flag by "
"using the next button <button 119/> and store it for further use."
msgstr ""
"Il pulsante <button 118/> permette di segnare un luogo con <a "
"object|flag>bandiere</a> di vari colori. Servono a non perdersi, a ritrovare"
" punti importanti o a indicare posizioni ai robot. Hai 5 bandiere per "
"ciascuno dei 5 colori. Puoi recuperare una bandiera con il pulsante "
"successivo <button 119/> e riutilizzarla."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/human.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Me</code>"
msgstr "<code>Me</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/huston.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 176/> Mission Control"
msgstr "<button 176/> Centro di controllo missione"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/huston.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "huston"
msgstr "huston"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/huston.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Earth control center for all <a object|human>your</a> space missions. Though"
" still named after the well-known mission control of the old days, "
"\"Houston\" is actually located in the middle of the Nevada Desert, the new "
"center for space exploration activities."
msgstr ""
"Il centro terrestre che controlla tutte le <a object|human>tue</a> missioni "
"spaziali. Pur conservando il nome dello storico centro di controllo, "
"«Houston» si trova oggi nel cuore del deserto del Nevada, nuovo fulcro delle"
" attività di esplorazione spaziale."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/huston.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Mission Control Center watches over you day and night, and a whole team "
"of scientists and engineers are working hard trying to find a solution to "
"all the problems that you encounter."
msgstr ""
"Il centro di controllo missione veglia su di te giorno e notte. Un’intera "
"squadra di scienziati e ingegneri lavora per risolvere tutti i problemi che "
"incontri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/huston.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Houston</code>"
msgstr "<code>Houston</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/key.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keys A, B, C and D"
msgstr "Chiavi A, B, C e D"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/key.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "key"
msgstr "key"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/key.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The keys give <a object|human>you</a> access to the <a "
"object|safe>vault</a>. You'll need 4 of them."
msgstr ""
"Le chiavi <a object|human>ti</a> permettono di aprire il <a "
"object|safe>deposito blindato</a>. Te ne servono 4."

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/key.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key A, blue and triangle-shaped"
msgstr "Chiave A, blu e triangolare"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/key.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key B, red and pentagon-shaped"
msgstr "Chiave B, rossa e pentagonale"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/key.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key C, green and shaped like a 6-pointed star"
msgstr "Chiave C, verde a forma di stella a 6 punte"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/key.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key D, yellow and circular"
msgstr "Chiave D, gialla e circolare"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../E/key.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Objects <a cbot|category>Category</a>"
msgstr "<a cbot|category>Categoria</a> degli oggetti"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/key.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>KeyA</code>, <code>KeyB</code>, <code>KeyC</code> and "
"<code>KeyD</code>"
msgstr ""
"<code>KeyA</code>, <code>KeyB</code>, <code>KeyC</code> e <code>KeyD</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/labo.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 166/> Autolab"
msgstr "<button 166/> Laboratorio automatico"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/labo.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "labo"
msgstr "labo"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/labo.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The lab is intended for the analysis of <a object|bullet>organic matter</a>."
" It will help <a object|human>you</a> become familiar with the insects' very"
" own technology and perhaps even use it to your advantage. Place a chunk of "
"<a object|bullet>organic matter</a> on the platform, select the lab, and "
"click the button corresponding to the desired research program."
msgstr ""
"Il laboratorio analizza la <a object|bullet>materia organica</a>. <a "
"object|human>Ti</a> permetterà di conoscere la tecnologia degli insetti e "
"forse di usarla a tuo vantaggio. Posa un campione di <a "
"object|bullet>materia organica</a> sulla piattaforma, seleziona il "
"laboratorio e premi il pulsante della ricerca desiderata."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/labo.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Organic matter."
msgstr "Materia organica."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/labo.txt:12 ../E/research.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "New and improved technologies."
msgstr "Tecnologie nuove e migliorate."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/labo.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "20 seconds."
msgstr "20 secondi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/labo.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AutoLab</code>"
msgstr "<code>AutoLab</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/lrv.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apollo Lunar Roving Vehicle"
msgstr "Veicolo lunare Apollo"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/lrv.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>< no archive picture available  ></code>"
msgstr "<code>< nessuna immagine d’archivio disponibile ></code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/lrv.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Lunar Jeep (LRV) was brought to the moon on July 30th 1971 by the "
"astronauts David Scott and Jim Irwin from Apollo mission 15. Its batteries "
"are still partly charged, which allows you to remote control it. But this "
"old-fashioned technology will be of no use to you."
msgstr ""
"Il veicolo lunare (LRV) fu portato sulla Luna il 30 luglio 1971 dagli "
"astronauti David Scott e Jim Irwin della missione Apollo 15. Le batterie "
"sono ancora parzialmente cariche, perciò puoi guidarlo a distanza. Questa "
"vecchia tecnologia, però, non ti sarà utile."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/mine.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mine"
msgstr "Mina"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/mine.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "mine"
msgstr "mine"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mine.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mines were a defensive weapons system used by the first expedition. Because "
"of the dangers this system causes for the mission itself, they are no longer"
" used in your expedition. In some exercises mines are used to learn how to "
"avoid obstacles. There is no way to remove them or to create new ones."
msgstr ""
"Le mine erano armi difensive usate dalla prima spedizione. Nella tua non si "
"usano più, perché mettono in pericolo la missione stessa. In alcuni esercizi"
" servono a imparare a evitare gli ostacoli. Non possono essere rimosse né "
"prodotte."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mine.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With a <a object|bottr>practice bot</a>, don't get any closer than 2 meters "
"to the position given by the instruction <a cbot|radar>radar</a>."
msgstr ""
"Con un <a object|bottr>robot da esercitazione</a>, non avvicinarti a meno di"
" 2 metri dalla posizione restituita dall’istruzione <a cbot|radar>radar</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mine.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Mine</code>"
msgstr "<code>Mine</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/mother.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alien Queen"
msgstr "Regina aliena"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/mother.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "mother"
msgstr "mother"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mother.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This huge insect is the mother of them all. It lays <a object|egg>eggs</a> "
"and from these eggs will hatch all the various kinds of insects <a "
"object|human>you</a>'re likely to encounter. All of them are extremely "
"hazardous to yourself and your mission. The queen's protective shell is "
"particularly resistant to attack."
msgstr ""
"Questo enorme insetto è la madre di tutti gli altri. Depone <a "
"object|egg>uova</a> da cui nascono le varie specie che <a "
"object|human>incontrerai</a>. Sono tutte estremamente pericolose per te e "
"per la missione. Il guscio della regina è particolarmente resistente agli "
"attacchi."

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/mother.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|ant>ants</a>"
msgstr "<a object|ant>formiche</a>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/mother.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|spider>spiders</a>"
msgstr "<a object|spider>ragni</a>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/mother.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|wasp>wasps</a>"
msgstr "<a object|wasp>vespe</a>"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../E/mother.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a object|worm>worms</a>"
msgstr "<a object|worm>vermi</a>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mother.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AlienQueen</code>"
msgstr "<code>AlienQueen</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/nest.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nest"
msgstr "Nido"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nest.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The alien nest is an odd structure out of which <a object|bullet>organic "
"matter</a> erupts on a regular basis. <a object|wasp>Wasps</a> visit nests "
"regularly to collect ammunition that they will use to bombard your bots, "
"buildings and yourself."
msgstr ""
"Il nido alieno è una strana struttura che emette regolarmente <a "
"object|bullet>materia organica</a>. Le <a object|wasp>vespe</a> lo visitano "
"per raccogliere munizioni con cui bombardare te, i robot e gli edifici."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nest.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AlienNest</code>"
msgstr "<code>AlienNest</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 170/> Nuclear Plant"
msgstr "<button 170/> Centrale nucleare"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "nuclear"
msgstr "nuclear"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The nuclear plant is a <a object|atomic>nuclear power cell</a> factory. It "
"transforms a chunk of <a object|uranore>uranium ore</a> into a <a "
"object|atomic>nuclear power cell</a> fully charged and ready for use."
msgstr ""
"La centrale nucleare produce <a object|atomic>batterie nucleari</a>. "
"Trasforma un pezzo di <a object|uranore>minerale di uranio</a> in una <a "
"object|atomic>batteria nucleare</a> completamente carica e pronta all’uso."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uranium ore."
msgstr "Minerale di uranio."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nuclear power cell."
msgstr "Batteria nucleare."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "30 seconds."
msgstr "30 secondi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/nuclear.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>NuclearPlant</code>"
msgstr "<code>NuclearPlant</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/power.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regular Power Cell"
msgstr "Batteria normale"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/power.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "power"
msgstr "power"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/power.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "A power cell supplies the bots and a few buildings with energy."
msgstr "Una batteria fornisce energia ai robot e ad alcuni edifici."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/power.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An entirely red power cell is empty. The green section indicates the "
"remaining capacity. A power cell can be recharged using a <a "
"object|station>power station</a>. A <a object|energy>power plant</a> is "
"needed to produce a new and fully charged power cell."
msgstr ""
"Una batteria completamente rossa è scarica; la parte verde indica la "
"capacità residua. Puoi ricaricarla in una <a object|station>centrale "
"elettrica</a>. Per produrne una nuova e completamente carica serve una <a "
"object|energy>fabbrica di batterie</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/power.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The capacity of a regular power cell is 100 times smaller than that of a <a "
"object|atomic>nuclear power cell</a> produced by a <a object|nuclear>nuclear"
" plant</a> using <a object|uranore>uranium ore</a>."
msgstr ""
"La capacità di una batteria normale è 100 volte inferiore a quella di una <a"
" object|atomic>batteria nucleare</a>, prodotta da una <a "
"object|nuclear>centrale nucleare</a> usando <a object|uranore>minerale di "
"uranio</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/power.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>PowerCell</code>"
msgstr "<code>PowerCell</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/radar.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 168/> Radar"
msgstr "<button 168/> Stazione radar"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/radar.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "radar"
msgstr "radar"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The radar indicates the direction of the nearest <a object|mother>enemy</a>."
" Moreover, the information given by the radar allows the mini-map at the "
"bottom right corner of your screen to show the position of all bots, "
"buildings and enemies as small squares and triangles of different colors."
msgstr ""
"Il radar indica la direzione del <a object|mother>nemico</a> più vicino. "
"Permette inoltre alla minimappa, nell’angolo inferiore destro dello schermo,"
" di mostrare la posizione di tutti i robot, edifici e nemici con piccoli "
"quadrati e triangoli colorati."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Radar stations also act as relays for communication with the Earth from "
"distant planets."
msgstr ""
"Le stazioni radar ritrasmettono anche le comunicazioni con la Terra dai "
"pianeti lontani."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information for the mini-map."
msgstr "Informazioni per la minimappa."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Constant."
msgstr "Continua."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/radar.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>RadarStation</code>"
msgstr "<code>RadarStation</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/repair.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 169/> Repair Center"
msgstr "<button 169/> Centro di riparazione"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/repair.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "repair"
msgstr "repair"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/repair.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The repair center regenerates the shield on damaged bots. A bot's shield "
"will absorb a certain amount of <a object|mother>enemy</a> hits. If there is"
" no shield left, this means that the bot itself, when hit next, will be "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""
"Il centro di riparazione rigenera lo scudo dei robot danneggiati. Lo scudo "
"assorbe un certo numero di colpi <a object|mother>nemici</a>. Quando è "
"esaurito, il colpo successivo distrugge il robot."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/repair.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Damaged bot."
msgstr "Robot danneggiato."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/repair.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repaired bot with regenerated shield."
msgstr "Robot riparato, con scudo rigenerato."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/repair.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few seconds depending on the repair job to be done."
msgstr "Pochi secondi, secondo l’entità della riparazione."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/repair.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>RepairCenter</code>"
msgstr "<code>RepairCenter</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/research.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 163/> Research Center"
msgstr "<button 163/> Centro di ricerca"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/research.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "research"
msgstr "research"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The research center is an enormous computer. Its most useful feature is its "
"ability to come up with new technologies as well as improvements on existing"
" ones regarding buildings and bots in particular."
msgstr ""
"Il centro di ricerca è un enorme computer. La sua funzione più utile è "
"sviluppare nuove tecnologie e migliorare quelle esistenti, soprattutto per "
"edifici e robot."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 65'536 processors it contains use up a large amount of energy.\n"
"Each research program necessitates a brand new and fully charged <a object|power>power cell</a>"
msgstr ""
"I suoi 65.536 processori consumano molta energia.\n"
"Ogni ricerca richiede una <a object|power>batteria</a> nuova e completamente carica"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat surface of at least 5 meters wide."
msgstr "Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante larga almeno 5 metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Request for research."
msgstr "Richiesta di ricerca."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:18 ../E/tower.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regular or nuclear power cell."
msgstr "Batteria normale o nucleare."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "Between 9 seconds and 1 minute depending on the research."
msgstr "Da 9 secondi a 1 minuto, secondo la ricerca."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/research.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>ResearchCenter</code>"
msgstr "<code>ResearchCenter</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/ruin.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ruin"
msgstr "Rovina"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/ruin.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A ruin is what's left of a building after it has been disabled by a <a "
"object|spider>spider</a> or by friendly fire."
msgstr ""
"Una rovina è ciò che rimane di un edificio distrutto da un <a "
"object|spider>ragno</a> o dal fuoco amico."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/ruin.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It can't be converted back into a reusable <a object|titan>titanium "
"cube</a>."
msgstr ""
"Non può essere riconvertita in un <a object|titan>cubo di titanio</a> "
"riutilizzabile."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/ruin.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Ruin</code>"
msgstr "<code>Ruin</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/safe.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 175/> Vault"
msgstr "<button 175/> Deposito blindato"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/safe.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "safe"
msgstr "safe"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/safe.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This dome-shaped building was conceived by the first expedition. Its purpose"
" was to offer protection to a new type of advanced bot. To protect it from "
"insect attacks, the vault was locked by 4 <a object|key>keys</a>. Only after"
" you find the 4 keys and place each one of them on their corresponding slots"
" will you be given access to the bot."
msgstr ""
"Questo edificio a cupola è stato progettato dalla prima spedizione per "
"proteggere un nuovo tipo di robot avanzato. Per metterlo al sicuro dagli "
"insetti, il deposito è stato chiuso con 4 <a object|key>chiavi</a>. Potrai "
"accedere al robot solo dopo averle trovate tutte e posate nei rispettivi "
"alloggiamenti."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/safe.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Vault</code>"
msgstr "<code>Vault</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/spider.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spider"
msgstr "Ragno"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/spider.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "spider"
msgstr "spider"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/spider.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Spiders work like suicide commandoes: whenever a spider gets within a close "
"enough range of its target, it inflates its abdomen and bursts into a "
"multitude of tiny burning fragments. These fragments will set fire to "
"everything they get in contact with. Luckily the spider won't survive."
msgstr ""
"I ragni sono assalitori suicidi: quando si avvicinano abbastanza al "
"bersaglio gonfiano l’addome ed esplodono in minuscoli frammenti "
"incandescenti, che incendiano tutto ciò che toccano. Fortunatamente anche il"
" ragno muore."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/spider.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AlienSpider</code>"
msgstr "<code>AlienSpider</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/start.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting Pad"
msgstr "Piattaforma di partenza"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/start.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "The starting pad is a platform used in some exercises. "
msgstr "La piattaforma di partenza viene usata in alcuni esercizi. "

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/start.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>StartArea</code>"
msgstr "<code>StartArea</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/station.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 164/> Power Station"
msgstr "<button 164/> Centrale elettrica"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/station.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "station"
msgstr "station"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The power station extracts energy from the underground and recharges <a "
"object|power>regular power cells</a> through induction. To recharge a power "
"cell loaded at the back of a bot, just move the bot to the center of the "
"platform and wait a few seconds. A <a object|power>power cell</a> carried at"
" arm's length can also be recharged. <a object|atomic>Nuclear power "
"cells</a> are non-rechargeable."
msgstr ""
"La centrale elettrica estrae energia dal sottosuolo e ricarica per induzione"
" le <a object|power>batterie normali</a>. Per ricaricare quella sul dorso di"
" un robot, portalo al centro della piattaforma e attendi qualche secondo. "
"Puoi ricaricare anche una <a object|power>batteria</a> tenuta dal braccio "
"del robot. Le <a object|atomic>batterie nucleari</a> non sono ricaricabili."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A power plant needs some energy in the subsoil. If the satellite report says"
" that energy is available only at some places, you will need a <a "
"object|botsr>sniffer bot</a> to prospect the subsoil. The marks it lays down"
" provide information about the specifics of its findings: a <a "
"object|enerspot>green cross</a> means that there is an energy deposit at "
"this location beneath the surface, which is indispensable to the "
"construction of a power station or a <a object|energy>power plant</a>."
msgstr ""
"La centrale richiede energia nel sottosuolo. Se il rapporto satellitare "
"indica che è disponibile solo in alcuni punti, usa un <a object|botsr>robot "
"rilevatore</a> per individuarli. Una <a object|enerspot>croce verde</a> "
"segnala un deposito sotterraneo di energia, indispensabile per costruire una"
" centrale elettrica o una <a object|energy>fabbrica di batterie</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The large power cell at the top of the station remaining red after the "
"construction is completed can only mean that the site is not geologically "
"adequate."
msgstr ""
"Se la grande batteria in cima alla centrale resta rossa dopo la costruzione,"
" il sito non è geologicamente adatto."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat and geologically adequate surface at least 6 meters wide."
msgstr ""
"Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante geologicamente adatta, larga almeno 6 "
"metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Empty power cell."
msgstr "Batteria scarica."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recharged power cell."
msgstr "Batteria ricaricata."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few seconds, depending on the capacity to be recharged."
msgstr "Pochi secondi, secondo la capacità da ricaricare."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/station.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>PowerStation</code>"
msgstr "<code>PowerStation</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/stonspot.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Underground Titanium Deposit"
msgstr "Giacimento sotterraneo di titanio"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/stonspot.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "stonspot"
msgstr "stonspot"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/stonspot.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A red cross reveals the presence of a stratum of <a object|titanore>titanium"
" ore</a> in the subsoil. It will be possible to extract it using a <a "
"object|derrick>derrick</a>."
msgstr ""
"Una croce rossa indica uno strato di <a object|titanore>minerale di "
"titanio</a> nel sottosuolo, estraibile con una <a object|derrick>torre di "
"estrazione</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/stonspot.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A <a object|botsr>sniffer</a> will lay down a red cross each time it "
"uncovers a deposit. <a object|botsr>Sniffer bots</a> can also detect the "
"presence of <a object|uranore>uranium ore</a> as indicated by a <a "
"object|uranspot>yellow circle</a> and of energy as indicated by a <a "
"object|enerspot>green cross</a>."
msgstr ""
"Un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> posa una croce rossa quando scopre "
"un giacimento. I <a object|botsr>robot rilevatori</a> trovano anche <a "
"object|uranore>minerale di uranio</a>, segnato da un <a "
"object|uranspot>cerchio giallo</a>, ed energia, segnata da una <a "
"object|enerspot>croce verde</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/stonspot.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>TitaniumSpot</code>"
msgstr "<code>TitaniumSpot</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/titan.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Titanium"
msgstr "Titanio"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/titan.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "titan"
msgstr "titan"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titan.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Titanium is indispensable for the construction of buildings, <a "
"object|factory>bots</a> and <a object|energy>regular power cells</a>. There "
"is usually some left on the <a object|base>spaceship</a> when you embark on "
"a new mission."
msgstr ""
"Il titanio è indispensabile per costruire edifici, <a "
"object|factory>robot</a> e <a object|energy>batterie normali</a>. Di solito "
"ne trovi una scorta sull’<a object|base>astronave</a> all’inizio di una "
"missione."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titan.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If more is needed, you'll have to <a object|convert>convert</a> chunks of <a"
" object|titanore>titanium ore</a> into usable titanium cubes."
msgstr ""
"Se ne serve altro, devi <a object|convert>convertire</a> i pezzi di <a "
"object|titanore>minerale di titanio</a> in cubi utilizzabili."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titan.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Titanium</code>"
msgstr "<code>Titanium</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/titanore.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Titanium Ore"
msgstr "Minerale di titanio"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/titanore.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "titanore"
msgstr "titanore"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titanore.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a object|titan>Titanium</a> is indispensable for the construction of "
"buildings, <a object|factory>bots</a> and <a object|energy>regular power "
"cells</a>. The titanium <a object|human>you</a> see in its usable, cube "
"shaped form has been <a object|convert>converted</a> from raw chunks of "
"titanium ore."
msgstr ""
"Il <a object|titan>titanio</a> è indispensabile per costruire edifici, <a "
"object|factory>robot</a> e <a object|energy>batterie normali</a>. I cubi che"
" <a object|human>vedi</a> sono stati <a object|convert>convertiti</a> a "
"partire dal minerale grezzo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titanore.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Titanium ore can be found either directly on the surface or in the subsoil. "
"In the latter case, it needs to be first located and identified by a <a "
"object|botsr>sniffer</a>, then extracted using a <a "
"object|derrick>derrick</a>. If a sniffer identifies a titanium ore deposit, "
"it lays down a <a object|stonspot>red cross</a>."
msgstr ""
"Il minerale di titanio si trova sulla superficie o nel sottosuolo. Nel "
"secondo caso va individuato con un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> ed "
"estratto con una <a object|derrick>torre di estrazione</a>. Quando rileva un"
" giacimento di titanio, il robot posa una <a object|stonspot>croce "
"rossa</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/titanore.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>TitaniumOre</code>"
msgstr "<code>TitaniumOre</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/tnt.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid " Explosive (TNT)"
msgstr " Esplosivo (TNT)"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/tnt.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "tnt"
msgstr "tnt"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tnt.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A TNT charge is extremely sensitive. You should approach it with caution so "
"as not to hit it or give it any kind of shock. The risk is minimized once "
"the explosive is within a <a object|botgr>grabber</a>'s grasp."
msgstr ""
"Una carica di TNT è estremamente sensibile. Avvicinati con cautela per non "
"urtarla o scuoterla. Il rischio si riduce quando l’esplosivo è nella presa "
"di un <a object|botgr>robot trasportatore</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tnt.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>TNT</code>"
msgstr "<code>TNT</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/tower.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 165/> Defense Tower"
msgstr "<button 165/> Torre difensiva"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/tower.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "tower"
msgstr "tower"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tower.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tower constitutes the best defense against <a object|mother>enemy</a> "
"attacks, whether they originate on the ground or from the skies."
msgstr ""
"La torre è la migliore difesa contro gli attacchi <a "
"object|mother>nemici</a>, sia da terra sia dall’aria."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tower.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tower requires either a <a object|power>regular</a> or a <a "
"object|atomic>nuclear</a> power cell. A regular power cell provides a "
"capacity for 8 shots. A nuclear power cell is of course preferable. The "
"tower starts blinking when it runs out of power."
msgstr ""
"La torre richiede una batteria <a object|power>normale</a> o <a "
"object|atomic>nucleare</a>. Una normale permette 8 colpi: una nucleare è "
"quindi preferibile. Quando esaurisce l’energia, la torre lampeggia."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tower.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The range is 40 meters. To visualize it, select the tower then hit the "
"<range> button <button 41/>. Red dots outline the circular zone for 20 "
"seconds."
msgstr ""
"La portata è di 40 metri. Per visualizzarla, seleziona la torre e premi il "
"pulsante <raggio> <button 41/>. Punti rossi delimitano la zona circolare per"
" 20 secondi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tower.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any flat surface of at least 3.5 meters wide."
msgstr "Qualsiasi superficie pianeggiante larga almeno 3,5 metri."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/tower.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>DefenseTower</code>"
msgstr "<code>DefenseTower</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/uranore.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uranium Ore"
msgstr "Minerale di uranio"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/uranore.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "uranore"
msgstr "uranore"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranore.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Uranium ore is essential to the production of <a object|atomic>nuclear power"
" cells</a>."
msgstr ""
"Il minerale di uranio è indispensabile per produrre <a "
"object|atomic>batterie nucleari</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranore.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is to be found on the surface or in the subsoil. In the latter case, it "
"needs to be first located and identified by a <a object|botsr>sniffer</a>, "
"then extracted using a <a object|derrick>derrick</a>. If a sniffer "
"identifies a deposit of uranium ore, it lays down a <a "
"object|uranspot>yellow circle</a>."
msgstr ""
"Si trova sulla superficie o nel sottosuolo. Nel secondo caso va individuato "
"con un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> ed estratto con una <a "
"object|derrick>torre di estrazione</a>. Quando rileva un giacimento di "
"uranio, il robot posa un <a object|uranspot>cerchio giallo</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranore.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A <a object|nuclear>nuclear plant</a> will then take care of converting the "
"chunk into a new and fully charged <a object|atomic>nuclear power cell</a>."
msgstr ""
"Una <a object|nuclear>centrale nucleare</a> trasforma poi il minerale in una"
" <a object|atomic>batteria nucleare</a> nuova e completamente carica."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranore.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All <a object|botgr>grabbers</a>. Due to its radioactivity, the <a "
"object|human>astronaut</a> can not transport it."
msgstr ""
"Tutti i <a object|botgr>robot trasportatori</a>. A causa della "
"radioattività, l’<a object|human>astronauta</a> non può trasportarlo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranore.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>UraniumOre</code>"
msgstr "<code>UraniumOre</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/uranspot.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid " Underground Uranium Deposit"
msgstr " Giacimento sotterraneo di uranio"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/uranspot.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "uranspot"
msgstr "uranspot"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranspot.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A yellow circle reveals the presence of a stratum of <a "
"object|uranore>uranium ore</a> in the subsoil. It will be possible to "
"extract it using a <a object|derrick>derrick</a>."
msgstr ""
"Un cerchio giallo indica uno strato di <a object|uranore>minerale di "
"uranio</a> nel sottosuolo, estraibile con una <a object|derrick>torre di "
"estrazione</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranspot.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A <a object|botsr>sniffer</a> will lay down a yellow circle each time it "
"uncovers a deposit. <a object|botsr>Sniffer bots</a> can also detect the "
"presence of <a object|titanore>titanium ore</a> as indicated by a <a "
"object|stonspot>red cross</a> and of energy as indicated by a <a "
"object|enerspot>green cross</a>."
msgstr ""
"Un <a object|botsr>robot rilevatore</a> posa un cerchio giallo quando scopre"
" un giacimento. I <a object|botsr>robot rilevatori</a> trovano anche <a "
"object|titanore>minerale di titanio</a>, segnato da una <a "
"object|stonspot>croce rossa</a>, ed energia, segnata da una <a "
"object|enerspot>croce verde</a>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/uranspot.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>UraniumSpot</code>"
msgstr "<code>UraniumSpot</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/wasp.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wasp"
msgstr "Vespa"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/wasp.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "wasp"
msgstr "wasp"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wasp.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The wasp is a formidable enemy, very hard to shoot down since its flying is "
"particularly swift. Wasps carry balls of <a object|bullet>organic matter</a>"
" that they will hurl at your bots and buildings and at yourself from above."
msgstr ""
"La vespa è un nemico temibile, difficile da abbattere perché vola molto "
"rapidamente. Trasporta sfere di <a object|bullet>materia organica</a> e le "
"scaglia dall’alto contro te, i robot e gli edifici."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wasp.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The <a object|tower>defense tower</a> is the easiest way to get rid of them."
msgstr ""
"La <a object|tower>torre difensiva</a> è il modo più semplice per "
"eliminarle."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wasp.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AlienWasp</code>"
msgstr "<code>AlienWasp</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/waypoint.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checkpoint"
msgstr "Punto di controllo"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/waypoint.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "waypoint"
msgstr "waypoint"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/waypoint.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the exercises, blue crosses indicate positions that have to be crossed. "
"They disappear as soon as a <a object|bottr>practice bot</a> crosses them."
msgstr ""
"Negli esercizi, le croci blu indicano posizioni da attraversare. Scompaiono "
"quando un <a object|bottr>robot da esercitazione</a> vi passa sopra."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/waypoint.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>WayPoint</code>"
msgstr "<code>WayPoint</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/worm.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Worm"
msgstr "Verme"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/worm.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "worm"
msgstr "worm"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/worm.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Worms transmit viruses to programmed bots. The virus alters the programming "
"to such an extent that the bot either functions in a very erratic way or "
"stops functioning altogether."
msgstr ""
"I vermi trasmettono virus ai robot programmati. I virus alterano il "
"programma al punto da renderne il comportamento imprevedibile o da bloccarlo"
" completamente."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/worm.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Worms live in the subsoil but sometimes emerge and crawl on the surface. "
"When they are underground they are undetectable and indestructible."
msgstr ""
"I vermi vivono nel sottosuolo, ma a volte emergono e strisciano in "
"superficie. Quando sono sottoterra non possono essere rilevati né distrutti."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/worm.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>AlienWorm</code>"
msgstr "<code>AlienWorm</code>"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/wreck.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Derelict bot"
msgstr "Robot distrutto"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wreck.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A derelict bot is what's left of a bot after it has been disabled by a <a "
"object|spider>spider</a> or by friendly fire."
msgstr ""
"Un robot distrutto è ciò che rimane dopo l’attacco di un <a "
"object|spider>ragno</a> o del fuoco amico."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wreck.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A <a object|botrecy>recycler</a> can convert a derelict bot back into a "
"reusable <a object|titan>titanium cube</a>."
msgstr ""
"Un <a object|botrecy>robot riciclatore</a> può trasformarlo in un <a "
"object|titan>cubo di titanio</a> riutilizzabile."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/wreck.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Wreck</code>"
msgstr "<code>Wreck</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/mother.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "It gives birth to the following insects :"
msgstr "Da essa nascono gli insetti seguenti:"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../E/destroy.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "<button 169/> Destroyer"
msgstr "<button 169/> Distruttore"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../E/destroy.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "destroy"
msgstr "destroy"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This building was designed to destroy objects. The object just needs to be "
"placed at the center of the platform and the button can be pressed. The "
"destroyer takes care of the rest."
msgstr ""
"Questo edificio distrugge gli oggetti. Basta posare l’oggetto al centro "
"della piattaforma e premere il pulsante: il distruttore farà il resto."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Object that is no longer needed."
msgstr "Oggetto non più necessario."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Satisfaction."
msgstr "Soddisfazione."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "5 seconds."
msgstr "5 secondi."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>Destroyer</code>"
msgstr "<code>Destroyer</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../E/destroy.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<a cbot>CBOT Language</a>, <a cbot|type>variables</a> and <a "
"cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr ""
"<a cbot>Linguaggio CBOT</a>, <a cbot|type>variabili</a> e <a "
"cbot|category>categorie</a>."

